Nicholas Cage woke up face-down in tall grass.

This was immediately suspicious.

He had fallen asleep in Las Vegas.

Las Vegas had grass, technically, but never this much of it and certainly not grass containing a small yellow mouse staring at him with the grave disappointment of an accountant who had discovered fraud.

Cage slowly raised his head.

“Hello.”

“Pika.”

Nicholas narrowed his eyes.

“You know who I am.”

“Pika?”

“Don’t play games with me.”

The creature tilted its head.

Nicholas Cage stood.

In the distance were rolling green hills, forests, a dirt road, and what appeared to be a twelve-year-old walking alone toward the wilderness accompanied by a fire-breathing lizard.

Nicholas took off his sunglasses.

He had not realized he was wearing sunglasses.

“Oh my God.”

He pointed dramatically toward the horizon.

“I’M IN POKÉMON.”

A flock of Pidgey exploded from a nearby tree.

Nicholas spun toward them.

“YES! FLY! WARN THEM!”

The Pikachu backed away.

