Twenty minutes later, Nicholas Cage encountered his first Pokémon Trainer.

The boy looked about ten.

“Hey, mister! Wanna battle?”

Nicholas stared at him.

“You’re challenging an adult stranger to ritual combat on a public road.”

“Yeah!”

Nicholas looked down at Pikachu.

Pikachu shrugged.

Nicholas crouched beside the child.

“What’s your name?”

“Ben.”

“Ben, listen carefully. Today you’re going to learn something more important than winning.”

Ben smiled.

“About friendship?”

“No.”

Nicholas stood.

“About escalation.”

He pointed at Pikachu.

“GO.”

Pikachu looked behind itself.

“Pika?”

“Yes, YOU. Destiny has selected you.”

Pikachu had not agreed to any of this.

Ben sent out a Squirtle.

Nicholas froze.

The Squirtle blinked.

Nicholas whispered, “Magnificent.”

“Squirtle!”

Nicholas slowly approached it.

Ben said, “Uh, we’re supposed to battle.”

“Look at him, Ben.”

“What?”

“Look at his tiny arms.”

Squirtle raised its tiny arms.

Nicholas’s eyes widened.

“This animal has chosen joy.”

Five minutes later, Nicholas Cage had forfeited the battle and was holding Squirtle like a newborn prince.

