By sunset, rumors had spread across the region.

There was a strange man.

He didn’t catch Pokémon.

Pokémon simply began following him.

Nobody understood why.

Nicholas had accumulated Pikachu, Squirtle, three Psyduck, a Slowpoke, and a furious Primeape that he referred to exclusively as “Mr. Business.”

When asked why he hadn’t put them into Poké Balls, Nicholas became visibly offended.

“You want me to imprison Mr. Business?”

Primeape screamed.

“LOOK AT HIM.”

Primeape punched a tree in half.

“He has dreams.”

