Within hours he had become convinced that the Pokémon world was an elaborate simulation.

His evidence consisted of:

1. Identical nurses.
2. Identical police officers.
3. Children wandering through forests without adult supervision.
4. Animals capable of altering weather patterns being stored inside baseball-sized devices.
5. Nobody seemed concerned about any of this.

Nicholas climbed onto the roof of the Pokémon Center.

“PEOPLE OF CERULEAN CITY!”

A crowd gathered.

“You think this is normal because YOU WERE BORN HERE.”

Pikachu sat beside him eating an apple.

“But I have seen another world!”

Someone shouted, “What’s it like?”

Nicholas paused.

“Worse in several ways!”

The crowd murmured.

“But that isn’t the point!”

He held up a Poké Ball.

“WHO BUILT THESE?”

Silence.

Nicholas slowly lowered it.

“Exactly.”

Professor Oak arrived the next morning.

⸻

Oak studied Nicholas for several hours.

“So you’re saying you come from another universe.”

“Yes.”

“And in your universe, Pokémon is a fictional franchise.”

Nicholas leaned forward.

“Yes.”

Oak leaned backward.

“And I am fictional.”

Nicholas whispered:

“Professor…”

He put a hand on Oak’s shoulder.

“You are crushing it.”

Oak became emotional.

“Thank you.”

Then Nicholas noticed something behind him.

A computer monitor.

On it was a strange repository containing diagrams, operators, graphs, and something labeled:

PANTHEON INTERMEDIATE REPRESENTATION.

Nicholas stared.

Professor Oak said, “Oh, that? Nobody knows what it does.”

Nicholas slowly approached the screen.

He began reading.

OBSERVE.

COMPARE.

BIND.

TRANSFORM.

GATE.

FEEDBACK.

His expression changed.

For perhaps the first time since arriving, Nicholas Cage became completely quiet.

Pikachu climbed onto the desk.

Nicholas whispered:

“This isn’t a Pokémon world.”

Oak blinked.

“What?”

Nicholas pointed at the screen.

“It’s a compiler.”

He began connecting things.

Evolution.

TRANSFORM.

Poké Balls.

BIND.

Type matchups.

CONSTRAINT.

Trainer battles.

SELECT → ACT → OBSERVE → UPDATE.

Experience points.

FEEDBACK.

Evolution stones.

TRIGGER.

Abilities.

GATE.

Professor Oak stared at him.

Nicholas’s eyes widened.

“Oh my God.”

“What?”

“The entire universe is running on game mechanics.”

Oak shrugged.

“Well… yes.”

Nicholas grabbed him by the shoulders.

“NO, PROFESSOR. LISTEN TO ME.”

Pikachu covered its ears.

“If we can decompile the mechanics…”

Nicholas pointed toward the world outside.

“…we can MOVE THEM.”

Oak’s eyes widened.

