Three days later Nicholas Cage had accidentally invented cross-domain Pokémon engineering.

They gave a Machamp the social mechanics of a dating simulator.

It became extremely emotionally available.

They gave Snorlax a stealth-game detection system.

It woke up whenever someone attempted to sneak past it.

They gave Magikarp the progression mechanics of an RPG protagonist.

Within seventeen minutes it had become an existential threat.

“TURN IT OFF!” Oak screamed.

“I’M TRYING!”

Level 94 Magikarp smashed through a laboratory wall.

“MAGIKARP!”

Nicholas pointed after it.

“YOU WERE GIVEN POWER WITHOUT WISDOM!”

The Magikarp used Splash.

Nothing happened.

Nicholas lowered his hand.

“…Perhaps I judged you too quickly.”

Then it leveled up.

The mountain behind them exploded.

